.SS "size_t stumpless_flatten_element_name (const struct \fBstumpless_entry\fP * entry, size_t element_index, char * destination, size_t size)"

.PP
Creates a journald-compliant name for the element\&. All lower case letters are converted to upper case\&. Characters that are not alphanumeric are replaced with an underscore character\&. This includes any UTF-8 characters\&.
.PP
If the destination buffer is too small to hold the complete name, then nothing is done\&. Callers can detect this by comparing the return value to the value provided in the size argument\&. If the return value is larger, then nothing was done\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Unsafe\fP This function is not thread safe\&. It reads fields of the entry and element without any synchronization\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Safe\fP This function is safe to call from signal handlers\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Safe\fP This function is safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled\&.
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
release v2\&.1\&.0
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIentry\fP The entry that the param is part of\&.
.br
\fIelement_index\fP The index of the element in the entry\&.
.br
\fIdestination\fP The buffer to write the name to\&.
.br
\fIsize\fP The maximum number of bytes to write to the destination buffer\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The number of bytes needed to write the complete flattened name, not including a NULL terminating character\&. If this is greater than size, then it signifies that nothing was done\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "size_t stumpless_flatten_param_name (const struct \fBstumpless_entry\fP * entry, size_t element_index, size_t param_index, char * destination, size_t size)"

.PP
Creates a name for the param by combining the element and param name\&. Both names are converted to all upper case and combined with an underscore character between them\&.
.PP
Characters that are not alphanumeric are replaced with an underscore character\&. This includes any UTF-8 characters\&.
.PP
If the destination buffer is too small to hold the complete name, then nothing is done\&. Callers can detect this by comparing the return value to the value provided in the size argument\&. If the return value is larger, then nothing was done by the call\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Unsafe\fP This function is not thread safe\&. It reads fields of the entry, element, and param without any synchronization\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Safe\fP This function is safe to call from signal handlers\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Safe\fP This function is safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled\&.
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
release v2\&.1\&.0
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIentry\fP The entry that the param is part of\&.
.br
\fIelement_index\fP The index of the element the param is part of\&.
.br
\fIparam_index\fP The index of the param within the element\&.
.br
\fIdestination\fP The buffer to write the name to\&.
.br
\fIsize\fP The maximum number of bytes to write to the destination buffer\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The number of bytes needed to write the complete flattened name, not including a NULL terminating character\&. If this is greater than size, then it signifies that nothing was done\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "struct \fBstumpless_target\fP * stumpless_open_journald_target (const char * name)"

.PP
Opens a journald target\&. This target will send log entries to the local service\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe race:name\fP This function is thread safe, of course assuming that name is not modified by any other threads during execution\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe heap\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the use of memory allocation functions\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe heap\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, as the memory allocation function may not be AC-Safe itself\&.
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
release v2\&.1\&.0
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIname\fP The name of the logging target\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The opened target if no error is encountered\&. In the event of an error, NULL is returned and an error code is set appropriately\&. 
.RE
.PP

